WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.490
A Raft cluster commits a write in a fixed order.

2
00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.800
Watch one write travel.

3
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.480
The client sends the write to the leader.

4
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.340
The leader appends it to its log,

5
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.800
then sends AppendEntries to each follower.

6
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.070
Follower 1 stores the entry and replies.

7
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.160
The leader and Follower 1 are two of three servers,

8
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.800
which is a majority.

9
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.260
The leader marks the entry committed,

10
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.050
applies it to its state machine, and replies to the client.

11
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.800
Followers learn the commit on the next message.

12
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.220
When a majority stored the entry, any new leader has it.

13
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.240
When only a minority stored it, the entry can be lost.

14
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.800
So the leader waits for a majority.
